From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Publish Q6DSP clock state before registering clocks

Registering a clock may reparent an orphan and prepare its new parent while
resuming a consumer. The prepare/vote callbacks use dev_get_drvdata(), so
publish the fully initialized controller before any clock registration.
Keep the allocation/devres order, firmware operations and clock tables intact.

The liuqin ADSP restart diagnostic reproduced the NULL dereference at
clk_q6dsp_prepare. A synchronous-reparenting C fixture fails on the original
probe and passes with early publication, including registration failures.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -146,6 +146,9 @@
 	cc->dev = dev;
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
+	/* Registration can prepare clocks while reparenting orphan consumers. */
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
 		unsigned int id = q6dsp_clks[i].clk_id;
 		struct clk_init_data init = {
@@ -178,8 +181,6 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
